> running debian woody on an alpha machine with kernel 2.4.18.
>
> Sep 13 11:59:12 lovecraft kernel: 16:03: rw=0, want=2101668,
> limit=2097648 Sep 13 11:59:12 lovecraft kernel: attempt to access beyond
> end of device Sep 13 11:59:13 lovecraft kernel: 16:03: rw=0,
> want=2101668, limit=2097648 Sep 13 11:59:13 lovecraft kernel: attempt to
> access beyond end of device Sep 13 11:59:15 lovecraft kernel: 16:03:
> rw=0, want=2101668, limit=2097648 Sep 13 11:59:15 lovecraft kernel:
> attempt to access beyond end of device
>
> Anyone have any ideas?

At is says, the disk has been asked to access something that is beyond the
end of the disk. There was a bug around for quite a while on Alpha (in
fdisk) that would allow you to partition one cylinder more than actually
existed on the disk. Don't know if Debian was hit by that or not.

