Dunno if this applies to you, but I had exactly the same problem on a=20
xl-300 using the built-in SCSI controller.  It turned out to be a result=20
of the particular CIA used in my machine (CIA version 1) and some code=20
change that came in around the 2.4.13 kernel and remains there in the=20
2.4.18 kernel. As far as I know, the 2.4.19 kernel isn't fixed either.=20
  For further details, see the thread on this list entitied "A SOLUTION:=20
Booting 2.4.18 kernel w/ sym53c8xx on XLT-300" dated 10 May 2002.

Jay Estabrook helped track this down and has created a patch for it.  I=20
have the 2.4.18 kernel working here now on my XL-300.  The "fix" I=20
described has been running since May without any noticable problems on=20
my machine.  You might check and see which CIA chipset your machine=20
uses, and if it is a version 1 chipset (21171) my solution might work=20
for you. Alternatively, send me an E-mail back channel and I will send=20
you Jay's patch that he developed.  You WILL have to re-compile the=20
kernel :(

Cheers,
-Don Spoon-


